{"id": "EUVD-2026-98674", "enisaUuid": "f353a79a-a61b-3f18-a84c-a0eccd38b7f8", "description": "Wazuh from 4.3.0 before 4.14.8 contains a remote code execution vulnerability where SCA policy trust is determined by file path rather than configuration source. Attackers controlling a manager can write unsigned policy files to var/incoming via the upgrade channel and reference them to execute command checks as root on agents.", "datePublished": "2026-10-13T13:27:29", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T13:48:46", "baseScore": 8.6, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:H/UI:N/VC:H/VI:H/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/wazuh/wazuh/security/advisories/GHSA-qmhg-366r-jjfp", "https://github.com/wazuh/wazuh/releases/tag/v4.14.8", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/wazuh-4.3.0-before-4.14.8-remote-code-execution-via-sca-command-policies"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-74036"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.83, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "bd7e68e5-3af9-3204-9853-9c927c306eff", "product": {"name": "wazuh-agent", "vendor": {"name": "wazuh"}}, "product_version": "4.3.0 <4.14.8"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b9e33606-329f-3503-9f3d-378977a4cc60", "vendor": {"name": "wazuh"}}], "isExploited": false}